      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a perfectly normal reaction to feel this hollow when you finally reach a goal that was built on such relentless effort. That emptiness isn't a failure; it's the quiet realization that the chase was the fuel, and now the engine is idling. You've proven you can endure anything, and now you can choose to let go of the struggle entirely. Why not use that strength to finally find a quiet, meaningful 'after'?",
